;; Cycle 09: cycle 08's findings folded in, cut as spec-12, then spec-13 when
;; the spec owner moved the oracle into one oracle.edn in one artifact pinned
;; by digest mid-cycle (tagged locally). The oracle group's builder was
;; stopped and its room fenced again from spec-13; the compliance and site
;; groups' rooms, fenced from spec-12, are kept: spec-12..spec-13 touches only
;; the oracle's feature, the glossary's oracle entry, the configuration, the
;; stack and the wiki, none of which their scopes read. The merge is based on
;; the spec-13 room.
;; Run by cycle 05's release; cycle 08's build is the cut's implementation.
;; Its scopes are what `rdm-spec scopes spec-11 spec-12` listed, plus two the
;; person judged the changed README reaches: kernel/command (the environment a
;; scenario's commands inherit) and spec/check (its step reads trace's result,
;; now a contract). The leftover run-time step registrations in components
;; outside these scopes wait for their next rebuild. Three builders in
;; parallel; the kernel's interface does not change.
{:cut "spec-13"
 :scope [{:context :compliance}
         {:component :kernel/command}
         {:component :knowledge/sources}
         {:component :measurement/oracle}
         {:component :publishing/site}
         {:component :spec/check}
         {:component :verification/release}
         {:component :verification/trace}]
 :builder {:name "builder subagents, one per group of scopes" :actor :agent}
 :grader {:name "grader subagents, each in its own grading room" :actor :agent}
 :spec-owner {:name "Sathish Narayanan" :actor :human}}
